vLLM 0.34 on ROCm: run the per-row MXFP8 linear (RocmDotScaledMxfp8LinearKernel)
through opaque custom ops.

_mxfp8_dot_scaled_linear / _mxfp8_dot_scaled_gemm choose the fused-quant branch
and the Triton tile (_select_cfg) from the token count M. Called straight from
the torch.compile'd forward, the choice is made once at trace time (the profile
run, M = max_num_batched_tokens) and frozen into every CUDA graph, so decode at
M = 256 ran the 128x128x256 prefill tile: grid 2x20 (qkv) / 2x16 (o_proj) on
MI355X's 256 CUs, ~18 us per call. Eager mode picks 64x64x512 (grid 4x40 / 4x32,
~10 us). The block32 path (rocm_block32_gemm.py) already uses opaque ops for the
same reason; this does the same for the per-row path. Numerics: same kernel and
MXFP8 format, only the tile changes.

Apply after vllm-0.34-rocm-mxfp8-block32-scales-switch.patch:
cd /workspace/vllm && git apply <this file>

